 "summary": "Commodities were broadly firmer in the latest session, with 12 of the 24 tracked benchmarks higher and 11 lower. Energy was mixed, 2 of 4 higher, the biggest move coming from Coal (Newcastle) at +2.19% to 144.85 USD/T; precious metals advanced across the board, led by Silver at +1.78% to 65.20 USD/t oz; base metals were mixed, 2 of 6 higher, the biggest move coming from Nickel at +1.75% to 16966.88 USD/T; bulk and battery materials were mixed, 3 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Iron Ore 62% Fe at +3.41% to 99.33 USD/T; agriculture fell across the board, led by Soybeans at -1.27% to 1290.11 USd/Bu. The largest single move across the complex was Iron Ore 62% Fe at +3.41%. Rare earths are represented by the MP Materials equity proxy, as no reliable daily spot benchmark is published. Reported alongside the session, Bitget on 01 September 2026:",
